# What this repository keeps, and what it does not.
#
# An ALLOWLIST, not a denylist: everything at the root is excluded and the parts
# worth versioning are named back in. A denylist here would be wrong — the
# working directory accumulates scans, crops, checkpoints and rendered pages
# faster than anyone can remember to exclude them, and the failure mode is
# silent: a 400 dpi column PNG committed once is in the history forever.
#
# John's rule, 2026-08-09: anything we can download again (the scan PDF) or
# generate again (review pages, crops, kraken checkpoints) stays out. The
# pipeline, the reader outputs and the corpus stay in.
#
# ⚠ AN ALLOWLIST FAILS SILENTLY IN THE OTHER DIRECTION TOO. The first version of
# this file kept out `pyproject.toml` — without which the package will not even
# install — along with five of the six readers' outputs, the persisted
# adversarial reviews, and the explainer. Nothing complained; they were simply
# not there. When adding a directory, check `git status --short --ignored`
# rather than assuming the rules below still cover it.

/*
!.gitignore
!*.md

# The package itself, and the resolved dependency set the tests ran against.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!bonitz_pipeline/
!tests/
!run_pilot_compare.py

# The explainer and anything else written to be read by a person.
!docs/

# EVERY reader's output, not just the adjudicator's. The whole method here is
# that independent readers disagree and the disagreement is the signal, so
# keeping only `opus` would throw away the evidence and leave the verdicts
# unfalsifiable.
!raw/

!work/
work/*
!work/reconciled/
!work/adjudicated/
!work/verdicts/
!work/damage/
!work/corrigenda/
!work/sigla/
!work/rulings/
!work/sweeps/
!work/lexcheck/
!work/recheck/
!work/prompts/
!work/flags-by-col/
!work/flags4-by-col/
!work/flags5-by-col/
!work/aristotle-forms.json

# The adversarial reviews, persisted deliberately: two finished ones were lost
# to a reboot on 2026-08-09 because they lived only in a temp directory, and a
# review nobody read is indistinguishable from a review nobody ran.
!work/reviews/

!work/kraken/
work/kraken/*
!work/kraken/NOTES.md

# Review pages are build artifacts and they are not small — book-review.html is
# 6.7 MB of base64 crops on its own. Every one regenerates from its module:
#   python3 -m bonitz_pipeline.mark_review    --html <path>
#   python3 -m bonitz_pipeline.book_review
#   python3 -m bonitz_pipeline.siglum_review
work/sweeps/*.html

# The rulings themselves are the point, and they are tiny. Keep them.
!work/sweeps/*.json
!work/sweeps/*.tsv
!work/sweeps/*.txt

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
